          "explanation": [
            {
              "text": "Disruptive selection changes relative reproductive success at both ends of a phenotypic distribution. Distinguish the favoured phenotypes from the resulting distribution: two favoured extremes can maintain variation instead of shifting the whole population toward one extreme.",
