      "heading": "Question 8 (b)",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "heading": null,
          "bullets": [
            "Disruptive selection was a well-known phenomenon but most answers stopped after stating that the two extremes of the distribution are selected for while the intermediates are selected against. Sketch graphs were often seen and needed to have their axes labelled to be useful."
          ]
        }
      ]
